/*
This file holds all weapon and mod categories, and a list of individual weapons that can be generated.

Each weapon category supports these keys (all optional except the name):
    "weight": 2                                  //Roll odds vs other categories. Omit for 1.
    "weapons": [ "id", ... ]                     //Hand-picked members. Empty/omitted with no selectors = ANY weapon.
    "requiredMods": [ "Mod Category", ... ]      //ALL listed mod categories required, any one mod from each satisfies it.
    "forbiddenMods": [ "Mod Category", ... ]     //Every mod in every listed category is forbidden.
    "calibers": [ "7.62x25", "9x19", "12g" ]     //DYNAMIC: every weapon of these calibers joins automatically at
                                                 //startup - including weapons added by OTHER MODS. Written the human
                                                 //way; matches internal names like Caliber762x25TT tolerantly.
    "excludeWeapons": [ "id", ... ]              //Hand-prune selector matches you don't want.
    "fireRate": { "above": 1000 }                //DYNAMIC: keep only weapons whose full-auto RPM is in range.
                                                 //"above"/"below" are strict bounds (either or both). It NARROWS:
                                                 //with "calibers" it filters those matches; alone, it filters the whole
                                                 //weapon pool. A gun with no fire rate (bolt-action, most shotguns) is
                                                 //excluded by any bound.

HOW MEMBERSHIP IS COMPUTED (resolved once at startup, against the LIVE item DB incl. other mods' guns):
    1. Start with the hand-listed "weapons".
    2. CANDIDATE POOL from "calibers" (a weapon joins if it matches ANY of them). If no "calibers",
       the candidate pool is EVERY weapon.
    3. NARROW by "fireRate": a candidate must be in range. So calibers and fire rate INTERSECT -
       "calibers:[9x19] + fireRate:{above:1000}" = 9x19 guns that are ALSO >1000 rpm, NOT 9x19 plus
       all high-rpm guns. (There is no OR/expand mode.)
    4. Prune "excludeWeapons", then merge the result into the hand-listed weapons.
A category with NO weapons and NO selectors is the deliberate "ANY weapon" shape (e.g. a "Suppressed"
category = empty + a required silencer = any gun with a silencer).

EQUIVALENCE (shiny/platform "counts-as" links, from weaponCompatibility + mods like ShinyAirdropGuns):
    A PURELY selector-based category (has selectors, NO hand-listed weapons) IGNORES equivalence - its
    membership is a live DB query, so a shiny/modded gun that belongs is already a direct member, and
    pulling in equivalents would only add guns the query excludes (a 9x19 platform-twin of a 5.56 member
    leaking into a "5.56" category). A hand-listed OR mixed category (any explicit "weapons") KEEPS
    equivalence: a shiny of a hand-picked gun isn't a direct member, so the "counts-as" link is what
    makes it count. (Pinned/vanilla weapon requirements always keep equivalence; that's decided per
    objective, not on the category.)
*/
{
    "categories": //Weapon categories
    {
        "Precision Sniping": //Name of the category that appears in-game.
        {
            "weight": 1, //How likely this is to appear, compared to other categories. Higher is likelier. The chance is the weight part of the sum of all weights.
            "weapons": //The weapons allowed in this category
            [
                "627e14b21713922ded6f2c15", //Accuracy International AXMC .338 LM bolt-action sniper rifle
                "588892092459774ac91d4b11", //Lobaev Arms DVL-10 7.62x51 bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5bfea6e90db834001b7347f3", //Remington Model 700 7.62x51 bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5bfd297f0db834001a669119", //Mosin 7.62x54R bolt-action rifle (Infantry)
                "5ae08f0a5acfc408fb1398a1", //Mosin 7.62x54R bolt-action rifle (Sniper)
                "55801eed4bdc2d89578b4588", //SV-98 7.62x54R bolt-action sniper rifle
                "673cab3e03c6a20581028bc1", //Sako TRG M10 .338 LM bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5df24cf80dee1b22f862e9bc" //ORSIS T-5000M 7.62x51 bolt-action sniper rifle
            ],
            /*
            The mod categories that must ALL appear on the weapon - one mod from each category
            counts (any silencer from Big Silencers, any bipod from Bipods, etc).
            So in total here, you have to have
            - A silencer
            - A Bipod
            - The Raptar
            all mounted to one of the weapons above.
            */
            "requiredMods": [ "Big Silencers", "Bipods", "Raptar" ]
        },
        "No scope": //Example of exclusive
        {
            "weight": 2,
            "weapons":
            [
                "627e14b21713922ded6f2c15", //Accuracy International AXMC .338 LM bolt-action sniper rifle
                "588892092459774ac91d4b11", //Lobaev Arms DVL-10 7.62x51 bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5bfea6e90db834001b7347f3", //Remington Model 700 7.62x51 bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5bfd297f0db834001a669119", //Mosin 7.62x54R bolt-action rifle (Infantry)
                "5ae08f0a5acfc408fb1398a1", //Mosin 7.62x54R bolt-action rifle (Sniper)
                "55801eed4bdc2d89578b4588", //SV-98 7.62x54R bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5df24cf80dee1b22f862e9bc", //ORSIS T-5000M 7.62x51 bolt-action sniper rifle
                "5de652c31b7e3716273428be", //Molot Arms VPO-215 Gornostay .366 TKM bolt-action rifle
                "5a38e6bac4a2826c6e06d79b" //TOZ-106 20ga bolt-action shotgun

            ],
            //Every mod in ANY of the categories below is forbidden from being used.
            //So this means you are effectively banned from using any optics. Iron sights are still allowed.
            "forbiddenMods": [ "Assault Scopes", "Optical Scopes", "Collimators", "Thermal Scopes", "Night Vision Scopes" ]
        },
